 3 - Circle of the Land Spells\n\nPagina: 84\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, choose one type of land: arid, polar, temperate, or tropical. Consult the table below that corresponds to the chosen type; you have the spells listed for your Druid level and lower prepared.\n\nDruid Level | Circle Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\nDruid Level | Circle Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\nDruid Level | Circle Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\nDruid Level | Circle Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Land's Aid\n\nPagina: 85\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape and choose a point within 60 feet of yourself. Vitality-giving flowers and life-draining thorns appear for a moment in a 10-foot-radius XPHB centered on that point. Each creature of your choice in the XPHB must make a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 2d6 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. One creature of your choice in that area regains 2d6 XPHB.\n\nThe damage and healing increase by 1d6 when you reach Druid levels 10 (3d6) and 14 (4d6).\n\nNivel 3 - Land's Aid\n\nNivel 6 - Land's Stride\n\nPagina: 68\n\nStarting at 6th level, moving through nonmagical difficult terrain costs you no extra movement. You can also pass through nonmagical plants without being slowed by them and without taking damage from them if they have thorns, spines, or a similar hazard.\n\nIn addition, you have advantage on saving throws against plants that are magically created or manipulated to impede movement, such as those created by the entangle spell.\n\nNivel 6 - Natural Recovery\n\nPagina: 85\n\nYou can cast one of the level 1+ spells that you have prepared from your Circle Spells feature without expending a spell slot, and you must finish a XPHB before you do so again.\n\nIn addition, when you finish a XPHB, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your Druid level (round up), and none of them can be level 6+. For example, if you're a level 6 Druid, you can recover up to three levels' worth of spell slots. You can recover a level 3 spell slot, a level 2 and a level 1 spell slot, or three level 1 spell slots. Once you recover spell slots with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Natural Recovery\n\nNivel 10 - Nature's Ward\n\nPagina: 68\n\nWhen you reach 10th level, you can't be charmed or frightened by elementals or fey, and you are immune to poison and disease.\n\nNivel 10 - Nature's Ward\n\nPagina: 85\n\nYou are immune to the XPHB condition, and you have XPHB to a damage type associated with your current land choice in the Circle Spells feature, as shown in the Nature's Ward table.\n\nLand Type | Resistance\n\nArid | Fire\n\nPolar | Cold\n\nTemperate | Lightning\n\nTropical | Poison\n\nNivel 10 - Nature's Ward\n\nNivel 10 - Nature's Ward\n\nNivel 14 - Nature's Sanctuary\n\nPagina: 68\n\nWhen you reach 14th level, creatures of the natural world sense your connection to nature and become hesitant to attack you. When a beast or plant creature attacks you, that creature must make a Wisdom saving throw against your druid spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature must choose a different target, or the attack automatically misses. On a successful save, the creature is immune to this effect for 24 hours.\n\nThe creature is aware of this effect before it makes its attack against you.\n\nNivel 14 - Nature's Sanctuary\n\nPagina: 86\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can expend a use of your Wild Shape and cause spectral trees and vines to appear in a 15-foot XPHB on the ground within 120 feet of yourself. They last there for 1 minute or until you have the XPHB condition or die. You and your allies have XPHB while in that area, and your allies gain the current XPHB of your Nature's Ward while there.\n\nAs a XPHB, you can move the XPHB up to 60 feet to ground within 120 feet of yourself.\n\nNivel 14 - Nature's Sanctuary"},
  ["feature.circle-of-the-land.xphb2024.druid.land.3"]={title="Circle of the Land",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 84\n\nCelebrate Connection to the Natural World\n\nThe Circle of the Land comprises mystics and sages who safeguard ancient knowledge and rites. These Druids meet within sacred circles of trees or standing stones to whisper primal secrets in Druidic. The circle's wisest members preside as the chief priests of their communities."},
  ["feature.circle-of-the-land-spells.xphb2024.druid.land.3"]={title="Circle of the Land Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 84\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, choose one type of land: arid, polar, temperate, or tropical. Consult the table below that corresponds to the chosen type; you have the spells listed for your Druid level and lower prepared.\n\nDruid Level | Circle Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\nDruid Level | Circle Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\nDruid Level | Circle Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\nDruid Level | Circle Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB"},
  ["subclass.circle-of-the-moon.phb2014.druid.moon.0"]={title="Circle of the Moon",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Circle Forms\n\nPagina: 69\n\nThe rites of your circle grant you the ability to transform into more dangerous animal forms. Starting at 2nd level, you can use your Wild Shape to transform into a bestiary (you ignore the Max. CR column of the Beast Shapes table, but must abide by the other limitations there).\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can transform into a beast with a challenge rating as high as your druid level divided by 3, rounded down.\n\nLevel | Max. CR | Limitations\n\n2nd | bestiary | No flying or swimming speed\n\n4th | bestiary | No flying speed\n\n6th | bestiary | No flying speed\n\n8th | bestiary | —\n\n9th | bestiary | —\n\n12th | bestiary | —\n\n15th | bestiary | —\n\n18th | bestiary | —\n\nNivel 2 - Circle of the Moon\n\nPagina: 69\n\nDruids of the Circle of the Moon are fierce guardians of the wilds. Their order gathers under the full moon to share news and trade warnings. They haunt the deepest parts of the wilderness, where they might go for weeks on end before crossing paths with another humanoid creature, let alone another druid.\n\nChangeable as the moon, a druid of this circle might prowl as a great cat one night, soar over the treetops as an eagle the next day, and crash through the undergrowth in bear form to drive off a trespassing monster. The wild is in the druid's blood.\n\nNivel 2 - Combat Wild Shape\n\nPagina: 69\n\nYou gain the ability to use Wild Shape on your turn as a bonus action, rather than as an action.\n\nAdditionally, while you are transformed by Wild Shape, you can use a bonus action to expend one spell slot to regain 1d8 hit points per level of the spell slot expended.\n\nNivel 3 - Circle Forms\n\nPagina: 86\n\nYou can channel lunar magic when you assume a Wild Shape form, granting you the benefits below.\n\nChallenge Rating\n\nThe maximum XPHB for the form equals your Druid level divided by 3 (round down).\n\nArmor Class\n\nUntil you leave the form, your AC equals 13 plus your Wisdom modifier if that total is higher than the Beast's AC.\n\nTemporary Hit Points\n\nYou gain a number of XPHB equal to three times your Druid level.\n\nNivel 3 - Circle Forms\n\nNivel 3 - Circle of the Moon\n\nNivel 3 - Circle of the Moon\n\nPagina: 86\n\nAdopt Animal Forms to Guard the Wilds\n\nDruids of the Circle of the Moon draw on lunar magic to transform themselves. Their order gathers under the moon to share news and perform rituals.\n\nChangeable as the moon, a Druid of this circle might prowl as a great cat one night, soar over the treetops as an eagle the next day, and then crash through undergrowth as a bear to drive off a trespassing monster. The wild is in the Druid's blood.\n\nNivel 3 - Circle of the Moon Spells\n\nPagina: 86\n\nWhen you reach a Druid level specified in the Circle of the Moon Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nIn addition, you can cast the spells from this feature while you're in a Wild Shape form.\n\nDruid Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\nNivel 6 - Improved Circle Forms\n\nPagina: 87\n\nWhile in a Wild Shape form, you gain the following benefits.\n\nLunar Radiance\n\nEach of your attacks in a Wild Shape form can deal its normal damage type or Radiant damage. You make this choice each time you hit with those attacks.\n\nIncreased Toughness\n\nYou can add your Wisdom modifier to your Constitution saving throws.\n\nNivel 6 - Improved Circle Forms\n\nNivel 6 - Primal Strike\n\nPagina: 69\n\nStarting at 6th level, your attacks in beast form count as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage.\n\nNivel 10 - Elemental Wild Shape\n\nPagina: 69\n\nAt 10th level, you can expend two uses of Wild Shape at the same time to transform into an air elemental, an earth elemental, a fire elemental, or a water elemental.\n\nNivel 10 - Moonlight Step\n\nPagina: 87\n\nYou magically transport yourself, reappearing amid a burst of moonlight. As a XPHB, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see, and you have XPHB on the next attack roll you make before the end of this turn.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB. You can also regain uses by expending a level 2+ spell slot for each use you want to restore (no action required).\n\nNivel 10 - Moonlight Step\n\nNivel 14 - Lunar Form\n\nPagina: 87\n\nThe power of the moon suffuses you, granting you the following benefits.\n\nImproved Lunar Radiance\n\nOnce per turn, you can deal an extra 2d10 Radiant damage to a target you hit with a Wild Shape form's attack.\n\nShared Moonlight\n\nWhenever you use Moonlight Step, you can also teleport one willing creature. That creature must be within 10 feet of you, and you teleport it to an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of your destination space.\n\nNivel 14 - Lunar Form\n\nNivel 14 - Thousand Forms\n\nPagina: 69\n\nBy 14th level, you have learned to use magic to alter your physical form in more subtle ways. You can cast the alter self spell at will."},
  ["feature.circle-of-the-moon.phb2014.druid.moon.2"]={title="Circle of the Moon",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 69\n\nDruids of the Circle of the Moon are fierce guardians of the wilds. Their order gathers under the full moon to share news and trade warnings. They haunt the deepest parts of the wilderness, where they might go for weeks on end before crossing paths with another humanoid creature, let alone another druid.\n\nChangeable as the moon, a druid of this circle might prowl as a great cat one night, soar over the treetops as an eagle the next day, and crash through the undergrowth in bear form to drive off a trespassing monster. The wild is in the druid's blood."},
  ["feature.circle-of-the-moon.phb2014.druid.moon.3"]={title="Circle of the Moon",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
